        },
        {
         "t": "heading",
         "level": "h2",
         "text": "What Should a Cleaning Business Logo Look Like?",
         "align": "left",
         "classes": []
        },
        {
         "t": "text",
         "html": "<p>A strong cleaning logo is bright, uncluttered and easy to read in a single glance. Customers often see it for a second or two: on a car parked in a Circle C driveway, on a door hanger in Pflugerville, or next to your rating on Google. Light blues, greens and crisp whites signal freshness, but the shape and lettering do most of the work.</p><p>The design also has to survive real-world use. It will be stitched onto shirts, printed small on invoices, and shown as a tiny square in search results. We keep icons simple, avoid thin lines that disappear in embroidery, and make sure your name and service stay readable everywhere.</p>",
         "align": "left",
         "classes": []
        },
        {
         "t": "list",
         "items": [
          {
           "text": "Clean shapes that hold up on shirts and aprons",
           "icon": "fas fa-check-circle"
          },
          {
           "text": "High contrast for vehicle magnets and yard signs",
           "icon": "fas fa-check-circle"
          },
          {
           "text": "A square icon version for Google and review sites",
           "icon": "fas fa-check-circle"
          }
         ],
         "classes": []
        }
       ]
      },
