       "t": "heading",
       "level": "h2",
       "text": "Cleaning Company Logo FAQs",
       "align": "center",
       "classes": []
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "accordion",
     "items": [
      {
       "q": "What colors are best for a cleaning company logo?",
       "a": "<p>Blues, greens and teals are popular because they suggest water, freshness and trust. Pairing one of them with white or a dark navy keeps the logo readable on uniforms and vehicles. We test colors in both print and embroidery before you approve.</p>"
      },
      {
       "q": "Should my cleaning logo include a broom, bubble or sparkle icon?",
       "a": "<p>It can, but those icons are common. A distinctive letter mark, a simple house shape or a custom character can help you stand out. We usually show a mix of literal and more unique concepts.</p>"
      },
      {
       "q": "Will my logo work for embroidery on shirts?",
       "a": "<p>Yes. We design with embroidery in mind and provide a simplified version without tiny details or thin lines, so it stitches cleanly at chest size.</p>"
      },
      {
       "q": "How much does a cleaning logo cost in Austin?",
       "a": "<p>Custom logo design at Logo Design Austin is priced from $125 to $175, depending on complexity, with no upfront payment. You pay after you approve the final logo.</p>"
      },
      {
       "q": "Can you also design car magnets and door hangers?",
       "a": "<p>Yes. Once your logo is final we can design vehicle magnets, door hangers, flyers and business cards that match it.</p>"
      },
      {
       "q": "What files do I receive?",
       "a": "<p>You receive vector files (AI, EPS, SVG and PDF) for printers and embroidery shops, plus transparent PNG files for your website, Google Business Profile and social media.</p>"
      }
     ],
     "classes": []
    }
   ]
  },
